## 📋 Complete Summary of All Backend Updates
### 1. AWS SES Integration (Primary Email Service)
- Replaced nodemailer with AWS SES in utils/sendMail.js
- Uses existing AWS credentials: AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID , AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY , AWS_REGION
- Sender Email : notify@bookby247.com (default, can override with SES_SENDER_EMAIL or EMAIL_FROM env vars)
- All existing email templates continue to work exactly as before
- Maintains queuing, concurrency, and fallback mechanisms
### 2. OTP Verification Email Template
- Created emailTemplates/otpVerification.js - simple black & white design
- Variables: {{ otp }} , {{ expiryMinutes }}
- Sender : no-reply@bookby247.com (configurable with OTP_SENDER_EMAIL env var)
- Includes copy button and hint text for better UX
### 3. OTP Channel Selection Feature (New!)
Users can now choose between email or sms for OTP verification.

APIs Updated:

- All APIs accept otpChannel parameter (values: "email" or "sms" )
- Default mode : email (if no otpChannel specified)
Which APIs Support This:

1. Auth OTP ( POST /api/auth/send-otp )
2. Inquiry OTP (inquiry related endpoints)
3. Appointment Booking OTP (public booking flow)
### 4. Frontend Changes Needed: For OTP Sending:
Add otpChannel parameter to your OTP request payloads:

```
// Option 1: Send OTP via Email (DEFAULT)
{
  email: "user@example.com",
  // otpChannel not needed - defaults to "email"
}

// OR

{
  phone: "9876543210",
  otpChannel: "email" // will send OTP to customer's email if available
}

// Option 2: Send OTP via SMS
{
  phone: "9876543210",
  otpChannel: "sms"
}
``` For OTP Verification:
Also updated to accept both phone and email for verification:

```
// Verify via Email
{
  email: "user@example.com",
  otp: "1234"
}

// Verify via Phone
{
  phone: "9876543210",
  otp: "1234"
}
```
### 5. Appointment Confirmation Template Fixed:
Updated appointmentController.js to pass all required variables to the template:

- Added: duration , amount , status , statusCheckUrl
- Both createAppointment and confirmAppointment functions now send complete data
### 6. Template Compilation Enhanced:
Updated compileTemplate in utils/sendMail.js to handle spaces in variables like {{ otp }} (not just {{otp}} )

